    t: 'Feeling acknowledgment, factual assent, diagnosis, and sanction separation',
    b: `FOUR SEPARATE ACTS. Acknowledge a reported feeling. Assess a factual allegation. Assess a diagnosis or causal story. Assess a proposed sanction or intervention. Agreement at one layer supplies no agreement at the others.

FAILURE MODE. Clinical affirmation or validation becomes gorgonified when it migrates into friendship, platform discourse, or AI response as a requirement to ratify the narrator's accusation, diagnosis, causal explanation, or desired punishment. Ritual agreement can turn one person's account into a settled social fact before evidence is assessed.

COUNTER-RISK. Reflexive disbelief performs the inverse error. Preserve the report, establish what the available evidence supports, distinguish unknown motive from visible conduct, and evaluate harm and intervention separately. Fidelity to the narrator's words remains separate from assent.`,
